            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The claimed invention relates to an upper for an article of footwear comprising a knit component forming at least a surface of the upper, wherein the knit component comprises a first surface and a second surface and one or more yarns extending between the first surface and the second surface. The one or more yarns form at least part of one or more of the first surface and the second surface. The claimed invention also provides an article of footwear, comprising a sole and an upper secured to the sole. The upper comprises a knit component forming at least a surface of the upper. The knit component comprises a first surface and a second surface and one or more yarns extending between the first surface and the second surface. The one or more yarns form at least part of one or more of the first surface and the second surface.</p>
